{"severity":"error","file":"errors/endpoints_label_invalid_2.march","start_line":11,"start_col":4,"end_line":11,"end_col":13,"message":"Protocol `P`: the label `msg_A_B_1` would name the message `Msg_A_B_1`, which is the shape of the names `@[endpoints]` makes up for unlabelled steps (`Msg_<From>_<To>_<k>`), so it could collide with one. Pick a label that does not start with `msg_`.","code":"endpoints_label_invalid","fix":null,"labels":[],"notes":[],"category":"PROTOCOL"}
